# Content

Interface text is part of the design system. Clinical users scan under
time pressure: write short, specific, front-loaded text, and write the
same thing the same way everywhere.

## Labels and casing

- Sentence case everywhere — headings, buttons, labels, tabs, badges.
  "Recent contacts", not "Recent Contacts".
- Field labels are nouns, short, and never punctuated: "Date of
  birth", not "Please enter the date of birth:".
- Do not use placeholder text as the label; placeholders show format
  examples only ("DD/MM/YYYY") and every field keeps a visible label.
- Abbreviate only what every user already reads as a word (NHS, GP,
  DOB in a dense table). When space allows, spell it out.
- Dates are day-first and unambiguous: "12 Mar 2026". Relative times
  ("2 hours ago") only for recency signals, always with the absolute
  time available.

## Buttons and actions

- Verb first, object when the verb alone is ambiguous: "Add to
  episode", "Remove from team", "Search patient" — not "Submit",
  "OK", or "Go".
- The primary action names the outcome of the screen; "Cancel" (not
  "Close") for abandoning a form mid-edit, "Close" for dismissing
  read-only surfaces.
- Destructive buttons say what is destroyed: "Remove team", "Delete
  record" — never bare "Delete" next to several candidates.
- One primary action per view; everything else is secondary, outline
  or ghost.

## Errors and warnings

- Structure: what happened, then what to do. "Referral could not be
  saved. Check the highlighted fields and try again."
- Never blame the user and never apologise theatrically — no "Oops!",
  no "Sorry!". State the fact plainly.
- Field errors name the rule, not just the failure: "Date of birth
  must be in the past", not "Invalid date".
- Match severity to the colour token: `--critical` text states harm
  or blockage ("Allergy information could not be loaded"), `--warning`
  states risk ("Results are more than 24 hours old"). Do not escalate
  wording for emphasis.

## Empty states

- Say what would be here and how it gets here: "No recent contacts.
  Contacts appear after the first episode activity."
- If the user can act, offer the action: "No teams yet. Add a team to
  start assigning referrals." — the action mirrors the button text.
- Distinguish *empty* from *filtered to nothing*: "No contacts match
  the selected date range." tells the user to widen the filter, not
  that the record is empty.
- Empty states are calm body text, not alerts — no state colour, no
  icon theatrics.
